<title>UK: Carrefour H1 profit higher.</title>
<headline>Carrefour H1 profit higher.</headline>
<text>
<p>NOTE - Carrefour said in a statement that the 936 million franc exceptional gain recorded for the first half of 1996 was due essentially to a capital gain from the sale of its stake in PriceCostco.</p>
<p>Pre-tax, pre-exceptional attributable rose 19.6 percent from the comparable year-earlier result. &quot;This performance reflects a rapid adaptation to changes in the economic environment and changes in management methods to adapt to the competitive international context,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
